title: Example - Markdown image - canonical URI
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki;vocab=Markdown

**Pattern:** `![](image-tiddler.svg)` referencing an image tiddler whose `_canonical_uri` field points to the external image URL (no base64 data in the text field).

This is the lazy-loading pattern: the wiki only stores metadata + a URL; the image itself is fetched from the network when the widget renders. Useful for large images or for keeping the wiki file small.

**Live example:**

![](Wikipedia Logo.svg)

**Source:**

```
![](Wikipedia Logo.svg)
```

**Why this works:** the source tiddler [Wikipedia Logo.svg](#Wikipedia Logo.svg) has `type: image/svg+xml`, no `text` field, and `_canonical_uri: https://upload.wikimedia.org/...`. TW's image widget chain:

1. Source is a known tiddler? Yes (`Wikipedia Logo.svg`).
2. Is it an image tiddler? Yes (the `type` is in the image family).
3. Does it have body text? No.
4. Does it have `_canonical_uri`? Yes — use that as the `<img src>` directly.

The browser then fetches the URL. The widget still honours the marker's `alt` and `tooltip` attributes from the same `attr-alt-from` / `attr-tooltip-from` wiring as the base64 case, so accessibility text stays correct regardless of where the bytes live.

